                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "41139036",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197979487649",
                            "num_reviews": 64,
                            "playtime_forever": 83,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 83,
                            "last_played": 1522357303
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A short, low budget point and click that has enough appeal to check out when on sale, although I wouldn't go as far as to really recommend it after writing down the following thoughts:\n\n+ The background graphics are nice\n+ The character design and animations are allright enough. \n+ Some nice usage of royalty free music (as mentioned in the credits).\n+ There's something interesting about the world and setting the story takes place in \n- But not enough is told or exposed to get you sucked in.\n- The sound effects are poor and don't really fit the game.\n- The dialogues are not very strong. The funny bits lack wit or intelligence, mostly just filled in with the word 'dumb' to be done with it.\n- The game is very short and straight forward. Not a lot of rooms, not a lot of objects objects of interaction. Even with as little locations as this game has there could have been more hot spots to be looked at and commented on by the main character, either adding to the lore or just for fun.\n\nI wouldn't mind to see more of this universe, in a more fleshed out form and on a broader scale. This game felt underdevelopped and like there might be more to it, at some time and place (and probably with a bigger budget).",
